                    quickbooks_deposit_account_id?: string;
                    /** @description QuickBooks Online deposit account name. Optional. Mutually exclusive with `quickbooks_deposit_account_id` — sending both is rejected. Omit both to use the company's Sales Deposit Account (see `quickbooks_deposit_account_id`). A name containing `:` is a sub-account's full name (`Parent:Child`) and matches that account exactly; it must itself be active and of type "Bank" or "Other Current Asset". Any other name matches among active "Bank" and "Other Current Asset" accounts: a top-level account with that name (its full name) wins; otherwise the one sub-account with that short name. A short name shared by several such sub-accounts is rejected with a message listing their full names — send the full name instead. When the top-level account with that name is inactive or of another type and a sub-account shares its name, the request is rejected with a message naming that sub-account's full name, rather than depositing to it. When your company is not connected to QuickBooks Online, sending this is rejected. */
